  "features": [
    "HTTP-thread snapshots capture request preparation, first incoming response header data, transport completion and encoded payload count.",
    "Fetch tasklets accumulate decoded delivered bytes under their mutex, convert monotonic timestamps relative to the VM origin, root temporary JS values and publish once on successful completion.",
    "Automatic HTTP/1 entries share global/Node timeline and observer identity; valid plain, streamed, gzip and canceled-body controls pass. Node HTTP adapter requests are not mislabeled as fetch."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "HTTP/2/3 producers, DNS/TLS/connection phases, complete redirect and informational-response timelines, failed requests, data/file fetches and partial-consumption accounting remain open under #873/#869. Missing milestones are not fabricated.",
    "The unchanged seven-file corpus retains the legacy zero-argument assertion failure #874; the scope is not green.",
    "The previously excluded constructor/Deno crash regression files remain unverified and were not rerun.",
    "Initial C++/Zig compile diagnostics, disk admission refusals and terminal cache cleanup are retained without passing credit. Both global-object producer outputs were preserved during pruning.",
    "Full Bun suite, remaining native/API ownership, Windows/Linux/ASAN/Release coverage and earlier ICU contradiction #872 remain open under #66."
